#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347563 #edb/ref 1080 "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, and $[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347563 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347563 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fa6e43ae-c189-5b22-9626-25bb56dbca9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347667 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347667 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347667 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347667 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347667 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347667 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347667 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347667 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186345662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347667 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "258c5139-84bb-595a-bdbc-339f120023e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347695 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347695 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347695 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347695 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347695 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347695 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347695 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347695 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186347563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347695 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "357ca7ee-2a06-5f79-91d3-044623ab8371" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77959" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1071 "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors $\\{i,j,k\\}$ of ${R}^{3}$ under the action of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bed05d64-8314-58af-9149-10494ba514ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348052 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ are the first, second, and third columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i,$ $T\\cdot j,$ and $T\\cdot k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T\\cdot k=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77990" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/20/20aff9b0dd1ea6aaab8cfa932317e83015956ac355349d5ae3d744de289bdae5.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $i$ and $j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$, while ${i}^{′}$ and ${j}^{′}$ are their images under the linear transformation $T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e54521b0-9af8-56df-9ce1-bb0fae27ed61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348054 #edb/ref 1074 "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that \n${i}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ \nand \n${j}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393772 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393772 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77996" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393772 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393772 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/2f/2f0c94bc3100b4fd9754ee822f55e2edbae8475bece3b18ac34f63e6c92267a2.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $i$ and $j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$, while ${i}^{′}$ and ${j}^{′}$ are their images under the linear transformation $T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393772 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8cfd1494-c300-5b47-97b2-4d30115ce6f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393772 #edb/ref 1074 "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that \n${i}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ \nand \n${j}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393773 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393773 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393773 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393773 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393773 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393773 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393773 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393773 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186393778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393773 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "747395f6-1977-5865-86f0-421323640a45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393774 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393774 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393774 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "69ef12c0-81b8-5e47-a65d-7cb7211c8786" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393775 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393775 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393775 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "001eef82-7933-51bb-851e-9e5adbffd169" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393776 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393776 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393776 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4220e4a4-2722-5a7e-ae00-ada68527f83b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393777 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393777 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393777 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b8383c7f-44a0-535e-b0ed-e0603eefcbbf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393778 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393778 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393778 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f8cdd350-9f6c-5b7e-9afa-c379f3ed1172" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403926 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403926 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77953" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403926 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403926 #edb/ref 1071 "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors ${i,j}$ of ${R}^{2}$ under the action of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403926 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6184324c-f65c-5086-93a0-7afae4b6be6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403926 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i$ and $T\\cdot j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403927 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403927 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403927 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403927 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403927 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403927 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403927 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403927 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186403931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403927 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fd1100a3-f46d-5e04-86d4-755b02a479bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403928 #edb/ref 1080 "$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403928 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403928 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "50e07024-23d2-5570-be5e-03b114b3c983" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403929 #edb/ref 1080 "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403929 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403929 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e0bbab46-dd35-5c94-a96c-8093cdf108d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403930 #edb/ref 1080 "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403930 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403930 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8e4bf657-7654-5279-9a17-d906a95a31d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403931 #edb/ref 1080 "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403931 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/r