#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476852 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476852 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476852 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476852 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186476602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476852 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d76409e5-f891-5850-b69c-49a2c2e9eb94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476902 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476902 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139994" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476902 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476902 #edb/ref 1071 "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors $\\{i,j,k\\}$ of ${R}^{3}$ under the action of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476902 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5ebff972-8ab2-5583-88cb-dd4e3c35dfe2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476902 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ are the first, second, and third columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i,$ $T\\cdot j,$ and $T\\cdot k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T\\cdot k=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
